{"content":[{"c":["SHEEP GATE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Jerusalem gate repaired by Eliashib and the priests under Nehemiah’s supervision during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.1,32","r":"Neh.3.1,32","rawR":"Neh.3.1,32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.1,32","value":"Neh.3.1,32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:1, 32"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.39","r":"Neh.12.39","rawR":"Neh.12.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.39","value":"Neh.12.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:39"},"). It was positioned east of the Fish Gate by the Tower of the Hundred, near the pool of Bethesda (Bethsaida) and a short distance from the modern St Stephen’s Gate. In ",{"href":"?bref=John.5.2","r":"John.5.2","rawR":"John.5.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.5.2","value":"John.5.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"John 5:2"}," the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," translates it “Sheep Market” and the ",{"c":["neb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", “Sheep-Pool.”"],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"SheepGate","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Neh 3:1, 32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.1,32","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.1,32","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.1,32"},{"anchorText":"12:39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.39","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.39","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.39"},{"anchorText":"John 5:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.5.2","rawQueryValue":"John.5.2","sourceRefExact":"John.5.2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"83589f005310dac02cc5bb86a247600b2a1f0aecea23d8afafcfe8803569d69b","sourceItemName":"SheepGate","sourceItemOrder":252,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"SheepGate","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"A